## 3. Canonical IDs & Two-Way Traceability Matrix (`Q3`, `Q12`)

Use one canonical identifier scheme across requirements, test plans, execution logs, and defect reports:
- **Acceptance Criteria IDs**: `{{ac_id_format}}` (and scenario IDs `{{scenario_id_format}}` where applicable)
- **Test Case IDs**: `{{case_id_format}}`

### Traceability Matrix Template

| Source Requirement / Guard | Linked Test Case IDs (`{{case_id_format}}`) | Proving Test Level (`Q5`) | Risk Tier (`Q8`) |
|---|---|---|---|
| `{{ac_id_example_1}}` | `{{tc_id_example_1}}`, `{{tc_id_example_2}}` | `api` / `ui` | `BLOCKER` |
| `{{ac_id_example_2}}` | `{{tc_id_example_3}}` | `visual` | `MAJOR` |
| `security-handoff:{{sr_id_example}}` (`SR14`) | `{{tc_id_example_4}}` | `api` | `BLOCKER` |
| `out-of-scope-guard` (`Q9`) | `{{tc_id_example_5}}` | `api` / `ui` | `MAJOR` |
| `regression` (`Q10`) | `{{tc_id_example_6}}` | `api` / `ui` | `MAJOR` |

### Traceability Invariants
1. **Forward completeness**: Every approved `{{ac_id_format}}` and BDD scenario maps to at least one `{{case_id_format}}`.
2. **Backward justification**: Every `{{case_id_format}}` cites either an `{{ac_id_format}}` or one of `security-handoff:<SR-ID>`, `out-of-scope-guard`, or `regression`. Orphan test cases are forbidden.

